Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g17: snapshot retained renders when firmware gives no blame

Base: rolotrealanis98/linux 8ab10100a4c1c944797e3fc8345589aff57777df

The J716s recovery at 2026-11-14 15:28:45 reported scheduling pause
firmware reason 5, no blamed queue, no sampled slot keys and four
retained Hyprland commands on queues 6 and 7. The existing bounded
render snapshot was skipped because it is only called for explicit
firmware blame. Queue ownership alone cannot show which render stage
had started, whether the backing manager was growing, or which
completion stamps had advanced.

Call the same snapshot before acknowledging recovery state 1, selecting
all retained render pairs when no QID was blamed. Walk pairs, not QIDs,
so each pair is reported once. Preserve the old exact-QID selection when
firmware does blame a queue. Only existing retained host mappings are
read; no allocation, new MMIO probe, scheduling change, timeout change,
attribution change or release decision is introduced. This is diagnostic
instrumentation, not a fix for the scheduling pause timeout.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/recovery.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/recovery.rs
@@ -117,2 +117,3 @@
-    /// Optional diagnostics only; absence cannot alter attribution or release.
-    fn report_blamed_render(&self, _qid: u8) {}
+    /// Optional halted-state diagnostics; None selects all retained render pairs.
+    /// Absence cannot alter attribution or release.
+    fn report_recovery_renders(&self, _qid: Option<u8>) {}
@@ -273,3 +274,1 @@
-    if let Some(qid) = request.blamed {
-        host.report_blamed_render(qid);
-    }
+    host.report_recovery_renders(request.blamed);
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/runtime/events.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/runtime/events.rs
@@ -276,1 +276,1 @@
-    fn report_blamed_render(&self, qid: u8) {
+    fn report_recovery_renders(&self, qid: Option<u8>) {
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/runtime/render/recovery.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g17/runtime/render/recovery.rs
@@ -9,1 +9,1 @@
-    pub(in crate::g17::runtime) fn report_render_recovery(&self, qid: u8, port: &crate::g17::port::Port) {
+    pub(in crate::g17::runtime) fn report_render_recovery(&self, qid: Option<u8>, port: &crate::g17::port::Port) {
@@ -13,1 +13,5 @@
-            entry.reservation.ids.iter().any(|id| id.qid() == qid)
+            qid.map_or_else(
+                || entry.borrowed_active || entry.constructing
+                    || entry.pair.as_ref().is_some_and(|pair| pair.in_flight()),
+                |qid| entry.reservation.ids.iter().any(|id| id.qid() == qid),
+            )
@@ -19,1 +23,1 @@
-                pr_warn!("G17: recovery render queue={} unavailable borrowed={} constructing={}\n",
+                pr_warn!("G17: recovery render queue={:?} unavailable borrowed={} constructing={}\n",
